  "fetched_at": "2026-08-19",
  "coverage": "Two real, structurally distinct slices of APiCS Online, both fetched live from the site's own server-rendered pages and DataTables JSON endpoints (never reconstructed from memory). (1) SURVEY CHAPTERS: all 74 of the 74 sociohistorical/grammatical survey chapters the site currently publishes (of APiCS's 76 named languages; 2 languages -- ids 21 and 51 -- have no survey chapter on the site, confirmed by the survey index itself listing exactly 74 rows) -- full prose sketches (introduction, sociohistorical background, sociolinguistic situation, phonology, noun phrase, verb phrase, sentences) each containing multiple real numbered interlinear-glossed example sentences (object-language line / morpheme gloss line / free translation) drawn from the contributing specialists' own published sources. This is a complete sub-collection, not a sample of it -- staged in full because the license is clearly open and 74 chapters (376,389 words total, min 1,928 words per chapter) is a bounded, session-fetchable set. (2) STRUCTURE/FEATURE-VALUE TABLES: a representative sample of 20 of the 76 languages' full primary structure datasets (130+ grammatical/lexical feature values each, with the exact value assigned to that language and its citation to the contributing specialist's source), chosen to span every one of the 9 lexifier groups (English, Dutch, Portuguese, Spanish, French, Bantu, Arabic, Malay, Other) and every region represented in the survey set -- NOT all 76 languages' feature tables, and not the site's separate example-sentence sub-dataset (18,500+ examples) or sociolinguistic/segment-inventory sub-tables, which were judged out of scope for a single bounded pass beyond what already appears embedded in the survey prose itself.",
